<!--
  Notion block mark, derived from the official notion-logo-block-main.svg.

  The official file layers a solid white background path under a black even-odd
  path. That works as a two-tone Image, but every place this project shows a
  connector mark uses Icon(tint = …), which flattens ALL paths to one colour —
  the white backing plate included, turning the logo into a featureless square.

  So only the even-odd path is kept: its outer square is filled, the inner area
  is punched out, and the "N" is filled again by the even-odd rule. That yields a
  single-colour silhouette with a transparent interior, which tints correctly and
  stays legible in both light and dark themes.
-->
